# EDGE AI OS sudo policy — base/prod tier.
#
# Members of the wheel group can run any command as any user.
# Password authentication is REQUIRED — no NOPASSWD: rule. Matches
# CRA's "no default authorization escalation" intent and the project
# rule that interactive admin work prompts.
#
# devel is added to wheel by edge-users.inc at image build time. To
# onboard another admin, add them to wheel, never to this file.

%wheel ALL=(ALL:ALL) ALL

# Convention: no other recipe in edge-* ships /etc/sudoers.d/. The one
# sanctioned exception is the bench override 15-edge-wheel-nopasswd,
# shipped by the edge-sudoers-nopasswd sub-package of THIS recipe and
# pulled into edge-image-dev only. sudo evaluates drop-ins in lexical
# order, last match wins per spec, so 15-… overrides the password
# requirement above only when the sub-package is installed.
# edge-image-base does NOT install it. Any other recipe that ships a
# drop-in here is a bug.
